 ## Website requests
 
+### Two-second prefill and boundary marker
+
+The latest 24-video set is in `audio-guided-prefill2s-comparison-20261028`, served
+at `/guided-prefill-comparison`. It repeats the same eight examples, checkpoints,
+seeds, native text policies, top-k/temperature settings, and full-model audio
+guidance from the earlier set, with exactly 25 source audio/pose/text frames.
+Every final video still lasts 60 seconds, including its two-second prefix.
+
+Text begins sampling at frame 25 for compact and original Xabi. Because media
+has a two-frame delay, the final two known audio/pose frames are supplied while
+those next text frames are sampled. Their temporal caches advance without media
+sampling. Thus no extra post-boundary source words are exposed, and the remaining
+727 media frames are generated with pose guidance. Saved input/output prefixes
+are compared directly against the source cache.
+
+After generation and rendering, final original/pose/overlay videos receive a
+two-frame white flash at 2.00 seconds and a quiet 100-ms, 880-Hz beep. All three
+views share the same marked soundtrack. `unmarked/` preserves clean videos;
+`prefill-marker.json` records hashes and boundary validation. The marker never
+changes model audio/codes, pose latents, or diffusion inputs. New request videos
+use the same presentation step. RGB rendering retains its existing clean sink
+and visual reference conditioning; the two-second prefill supplies the PPM's
+audio, pose, and text inputs.
+
+### Audio-guided native comparison
+
+The separate `audio-guided-native-comparison-20261028` run uses the same eight
+60-second examples with each checkpoint's native text format: aligned-media
+receives the full aligned prefix and forced framewise words; compact-all
+receives the ordinary full transcript and samples words; original Xabi receives
+the voice/system prefix and samples words without a transcript. All temperatures
+are 1. Audio top-k is 30 for every codebook; pose top-k is 30 for cb0 and 50 for
+cb1–31. Text top-k remains 0 (unfiltered).
+
+`--pose-audio-guidance 3` applies `audio + 3 * (audio - silence)` to every pose
+codebook's logits before top-k filtering. This corresponds to the engine's
+`pose_cfg_s=4` convention. The second branch has independent backbone, pose-tower,
+and pose-decoder caches, including its own backbone-to-decoder hidden projection.
+Every audio code, including the voice prefix and generated history, is replaced
+with codes produced by the pinned Mimi codec from digital silence. Both branches
+receive identical text, pose history, and sampled pose prefixes within each frame.
+Audio and text are sampled from the ordinary conditional branch.
+
+Both `infer.py` and `infer_batch.py` accept these settings:
+
+```bash
+--audio-topk 30 --pose-topk 30 --pose-light-topk 50 --pose-audio-guidance 3
+```
+
+Each output saves the silence codes, their hash, the exact sampling settings,
+and a guidance audit covering independent caches and the number of guided frames.
+The website's separate `/guided-comparison` page shows the three models alongside
+their supplied conditioning and generated text; existing comparisons are retained.
